    <fr:title text="Derivation / parse tree animation macros">Derivation / parse tree animation macros</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Authoring layer for animated derivation trees, rendered by <html:code>dtree.js</html:code>.
One tree, two views: <html:code>dtreeParse</html:code> draws a parse tree (nodes + edges, grows
down); <html:code>dtreeInf</html:code> draws the same tree as an inference-rule derivation
(rule bars, grows up). The structure is shared --- a node carries a rule name,
a conclusion (judgment), and ordered children (sub-derivations and terminal
tokens).</html:p>
    <html:p>Spec-driven variants: the tree is GENERATED from a real inductive term (e.g.
Agda's <html:code>toSpec : DyckAST -&gt; String</html:code>) and embedded as a JSON spec. Pass the
JSON via <html:code><![CDATA[...]]></html:code> so its braces are not parsed by Forester.</html:p>
    <html:p>Keyframe animation: several tree states (each a <html:code>dkf</html:code> JSON spec). Nodes
are matched by <html:code>id</html:code> across keyframes; reordering or regrouping children
makes them glide, with edges/bars re-derived each frame. Loops by default.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
